---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
---

<Docs
	page="configuration"
	title="Configuration"
	lede="Every option, where it comes from, and which layer wins."
>
	<section>
		<h2>Where settings come from</h2>
		<p>
			squill reads the nearest <code>squill.toml</code> (or{" "}
			<code>.config/squill.toml</code>) at or above each file it formats, and
			flags override it. The defaults are the house style; everything is
			optional, and a project with no config file is a supported setup.
		</p>
		<p>
			The search upward stops at a git repository root, a mount point, or a
			symlinked directory. A stray config in a scratch directory or a home
			directory therefore never reaches inside a checkout &mdash; if a config
			governs your file, it lives in your project.
		</p>
		<div class="note">
			<p>
				Layers, lowest first: built-in defaults, the config file&rsquo;s
				top-level keys, its <code>[language]</code> section for the file being
				formatted, then command-line flags.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Options</h2>
		<p>
			Every key has a matching flag. Keys are what you put in{" "}
			<code>squill.toml</code>; flags win over both config layers.
		</p>
		<div class="scroll">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr><th>key</th><th>flag</th><th>values</th><th>default</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<td><code>dialect</code></td>
						<td><code>--dialect</code></td>
						<td><code>postgres</code> | <code>sqlite</code></td>
						<td><code>postgres</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>indent</code></td>
						<td><code>--indent</code></td>
						<td><code>tab</code> | <code>spaces</code></td>
						<td><code>tab</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>indent-width</code></td>
						<td><code>--indent-width</code></td>
						<td>width of one level, and the measure of a tab; 1 to 16</td>
						<td><code>2</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>max-width</code></td>
						<td><code>--max-width</code></td>
						<td>target line width, 20 to 500</td>
						<td><code>80</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>keyword-case</code></td>
						<td><code>--keyword-case</code></td>
						<td><code>lower</code> | <code>upper</code></td>
						<td><code>lower</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>quote-idents</code></td>
						<td><code>--quote-idents</code></td>
						<td><code>as-needed</code> | <code>always</code></td>
						<td><code>as-needed</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>at-params</code></td>
						<td><code>--at-params</code></td>
						<td
							>lex <a
								href="https://docs.sqlc.dev/en/latest/howto/named_parameters.html"
								>sqlc-style</a
							> <code>@name</code> parameters</td
						>
						<td><code>false</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>ignore</code></td>
						<td><code>--ignore</code></td>
						<td>glob patterns to skip when recursing</td>
						<td><code>[]</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>frozen</code></td>
						<td><code>--frozen</code></td>
						<td
							>glob patterns that are immutable once on the baseline ref (see{" "}
							<a href="docs/frozen/">frozen paths</a>)</td
						>
						<td><code>[]</code></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>frozen-ref</code></td>
						<td><code>--frozen-ref</code></td>
						<td>the baseline ref <code>frozen</code> compares against</td>
						<td>discovered from the remote</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>frozen-fetch</code></td>
						<td><code>--frozen-fetch</code></td>
						<td>let <code>frozen</code> fetch the remote&rsquo;s HEAD</td>
						<td><code>false</code></td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>
			Flags with no config key: <code>--check</code>, <code>--stdin</code> /
			<code>--stdout</code>, <code>--strict</code>, <code>--no-config</code>,{" "}
			<code>--embedded</code>, <code>--embedded-query</code>,{" "}
			<code>--version</code>, and <code>--help</code>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Skipping files</h2>
		<p>
			When recursing directories squill honors <code>.gitignore</code> and skips
			hidden files. <code>ignore</code> skips more, with <code>*</code>,{" "}
			<code>**</code>, <code>?</code>, <code>[abc]</code>, and{" "}
			<code>&lbrace;a,b&rbrace;</code> glob syntax. Patterns are relative to the
			config file that declares them.
		</p>
		<pre><code>ignore = ["legacy/**", "*.gen.sql"]</code></pre>
		<p>
			A file named explicitly on the command line always formats, ignore
			patterns included &mdash; if you asked for that file by name, you meant
			it. <a href="docs/frozen/">Frozen paths</a> are the deliberate exception.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Per-language sections</h2>
		<p>
			SQL embedded in host code copies that file&rsquo;s own indent character,
			so a spaces-indented file never gains tabs. To choose deliberately, add a
			section named for the host language. It takes the same keys as the top
			level and overrides them for files of that language, so one config can
			ask for two spaces in JavaScript and tabs in Go.
		</p>
		<pre><code>indent = "tab"

[javascript]
indent = "spaces"
indent-width = 2

[python]
dialect = "sqlite"
indent = "spaces"
indent-width = 4</code></pre>
		<p>Each section covers one host language:</p>
		<div class="scroll">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr><th>section</th><th>files</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr><td><code>[rust]</code></td><td><code>.rs</code></td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>[go]</code></td><td><code>.go</code></td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>[python]</code></td><td><code>.py</code></td></tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>[javascript]</code></td>
						<td>
							<code>.js</code> <code>.jsx</code> <code>.mjs</code>{" "}
							<code>.cjs</code>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td><code>[typescript]</code></td>
						<td>
							<code>.ts</code> <code>.tsx</code> <code>.mts</code>{" "}
							<code>.cts</code>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr><td><code>[gleam]</code></td><td><code>.gleam</code></td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p>
			JavaScript and TypeScript are split only because they need different
			grammars; each section covers its whole family.
		</p>
		<p>
			One section can name several languages, comma separated. TOML has no bare
			comma in a table header, so quote the list:
		</p>
		<pre><code>["javascript, typescript"]
indent = "spaces"
indent-width = 2</code></pre>
		<p>
			The path-scoped keys &mdash; <code>ignore</code>, <code>frozen</code>,{" "}
			<code>frozen-ref</code>, and <code>frozen-fetch</code> &mdash; apply to
			the whole config file, so they stay at the top level. Naming an unknown
			language, or claiming one from two sections, is an error with a line
			number rather than a silent surprise.
		</p>
	</section>
</Docs>
